{
  "about": "Vectors for the host label (DEC-0154 item 4), written by tools/vectors/host-label.ts, never by hand. hostLabel(input): input is {platform, secret: {link, owner, writableByOthers, folderOk, hex}, orgId}: platform posix or windows; link whether the path is a symbolic link (a reparse point); owner root (uid 0), administrators (the Windows Administrators group), system (Windows SYSTEM) or other, the administrator being root on posix and administrators or system on windows; writableByOthers whether anyone but the platform's administrator may write the file (on posix any write permission, mode bits or an ACL entry, for anyone but root; on windows an ACE granting write to a SID other than Administrators or SYSTEM); folderOk whether its folder is the administrator's and writable by no one but the platform's administrator; hex the file's bytes in lower-case hex, read only when the metadata passes (so absent or empty otherwise), up to 1024 bytes checked for size and a fault above; orgId the enrollment's org.id. The answer is {hostLabel}: HMAC-SHA-256 keyed with the 32-byte secret over the UTF-8 bytes of fabric-host-label/1 followed directly by orgId, its first 16 bytes in base64url without padding; or {none: secret-link | secret-owner | secret-mode | secret-size}, the first reason in that order, the node sending no label; or {fault: input-invalid}: a fault in the shape of the platform, the owner name, a flag or orgId outranks every none; the size of the bytes is read only after link, owner and mode.",
